@startuml transient-vs-sustained
title US-04: Transient vs Sustained - Single Ping Does Not Alert, Sustained Deviation Does

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "TimescaleDB\nroute_baseline" as Baseline
database "Redis\ndeviation-state:{id}" as DevState
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Transient ping outside baseline (no alert) ==

Evaluator -> Redis : fetch current position of entity DEF
Redis --> Evaluator : position outside baseline by 45 km

Evaluator -> DevState : INCR deviation-counter:DEF
DevState --> Evaluator : counter = 1

Evaluator -> Evaluator : counter < SUSTAINED_DEVIATION_CYCLES\nno alert emitted

note over Evaluator
  A single ping outside the baseline
  could be a GPS glitch or brief correction.
  Not actionable on its own.
end note

== Next cycle: back within baseline ==

Evaluator -> Redis : fetch current position of entity DEF
Redis --> Evaluator : position within baseline

Evaluator -> DevState : DEL deviation-counter:DEF
note over Evaluator
  Counter reset. Transient - no alert raised.
end note

== Sustained deviation (alert emitted) ==

loop for N consecutive cycles
  Evaluator -> Redis : fetch current position of entity DEF
  Redis --> Evaluator : position outside baseline by 45 km
  Evaluator -> DevState : INCR deviation-counter:DEF
end

DevState --> Evaluator : counter >= SUSTAINED_DEVIATION_CYCLES

Evaluator -> Baseline : confirm baseline for this time bucket
Baseline --> Evaluator : expected position range

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish ROUTE_DEVIATION alert\n{ entity_id, current_position,\n  baseline_position, deviation_metres,\n  sustained_cycles }

@enduml
